   "startMs": 33630,
   "endMs": 55364,
   "startSecond": 33.63,
   "endSecond": 55.364,
   "narrativeScript": "That's a race condition. Counter plus plus is really three steps: read, add, write. The fix? Make them one unbreakable step. Wrap it in a lock. One thread holds the lock, the other waits. Now two increments really give two. Who's guarding your door? Send this to a Java friend who skips the lock.",
